# Addresses whose lane offsets or trip shifts pass 2^63 bytes: summed in
# i64 they overflowed and a debug build panicked. A lane or loop part
# past 2^62 bytes is now left uncounted: the warp's sectors are unknown,
# and the loop's unique bytes, though ptxas stores 4 B on each of 8
# distinct addresses.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/offsets_wide.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd4], %r1; // global store [18014398509481984·%tid.x + param_0] sectors/req ? (lane offsets reach 2^62 bytes){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB1_1: // loop: trips 8 | global per CTA: requested 32 B, unique ? | warp * × lane * | exec 8/CTA{{$}}
